diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -608,3 +608,25 @@
 Do not repeat what the codebase already shows; point to the authoritative file, skill, command, or doc.
 Prefer rewriting or pruning existing entries over appending new ones.
 When updating this file, preserve every safety boundary and keep the always-loaded contract concise.
+
+## Saved Orchflows intake and publication
+
+FirstMate's optional workflow home defaults to $FM_HOME/data/.orchflows-home.
+Use bin/fm-orchflows-home.py --home "$FM_HOME" setup --package <fork-package>
+once, or pass --package on the first publish. An explicit --workflow-home or
+ORCHFLOWS_FIRSTMATE_HOME selects another home without editing active tasks.
+Use its catalog and resolve <library:skill> commands at intake. Select an
+available workflow with fm-brief.sh <task> <repo> --scout|--mode local-only
+--orchflows-skill <library:skill>; normal spawn retains its complete libraries,
+selected instructions and declared composition. This does not admit no-mistakes
+or give a worker fleet-supervisor authority.
+
+For "create and save", have the worker author and trial a complete ordinary
+library in its assigned project, then deliver through the existing root owners.
+After delivery, FirstMate runs one publication operation:
+bin/fm-orchflows-home.py --home "$FM_HOME" publish --project <project-path>
+--library <relative-library-directory> --commit <exact-delivered-commit>.
+It copies regular Git blobs reachable from local default, refreshes package
+catalogs and future selected bundles, and preserves active task snapshots.
+Workers must report their delivered library location and commit; they do not
+write into the editable home or run its setup/publish owner.
